\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\title{Degree scaling and the paired top coefficient}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{A massless cochain operator exchanges even and odd cell
degrees. Scaling their generators in opposite directions can
preserve its quadratic element while changing the top
coefficient. The finite Euler count determines that change
on any finite cell model with a free coefficient fiber.}

